      "line_start": null,
      "page": 95,
      "row": null,
      "source_digest": "sha256:a216fe199bd6e9c77fc743dfe6dc081ee5f245adcb115ed6ca1aa45ee50fa3f5",
      "source_file": "ASD-STE100_ISSUE9.txt"
    }
  },
  {
    "requirement": "Use an applicable word (for example, “warning” or “caution”) to identify the level of risk.",
    "rule_id": "7.1",
    "source": {
      "line_end": null,
      "line_start": null,
      "page": 103,
      "row": null,
      "source_digest": "sha256:a216fe199bd6e9c77fc743dfe6dc081ee5f245adcb115ed6ca1aa45ee50fa3f5",
      "source_file": "ASD-STE100_ISSUE9.txt"
    }
  },
  {
    "requirement": "Start a safety instruction with a clear and accurate command or condition.",
    "rule_id": "7.2",
    "source": {
      "line_end": null,
      "line_start": null,
      "page": 103,
      "row": null,
      "source_digest": "sha256:a216fe199bd6e9c77fc743dfe6dc081ee5f245adcb115ed6ca1aa45ee50fa3f5",
      "source_file": "ASD-STE100_ISSUE9.txt"
    }
  },
  {
    "requirement": "Give an explanation to show the risk or possible result.",
    "rule_id": "7.3",
    "source": {
      "line_end": null,
      "line_start": null,
      "page": 103,
      "row": null,
      "source_digest": "sha256:a216fe199bd6e9c77fc743dfe6dc081ee5f245adcb115ed6ca1aa45ee50fa3f5",
      "source_file": "ASD-STE100_ISSUE9.txt"
    }
  },
  {
    "requirement": "You can use all standard English punctuation marks but not the semicolon (;).",
    "rule_id": "8.1",
    "source": {
      "line_end": null,
      "line_start": null,
      "page": 107,
      "row": null,
      "source_digest": "sha256:a216fe199bd6e9c77fc743dfe6dc081ee5f245adcb115ed6ca1aa45ee50fa3f5",
      "source_file": "ASD-STE100_ISSUE9.txt"
    }
  },
  {
    "requirement": "Use hyphens (-) to connect words that are directly related.",
    "rule_id": "8.2",
    "source": {
      "line_end": null,
      "line_start": null,
      "page": 107,
      "row": null,
      "source_digest": "sha256:a216fe199bd6e9c77fc743dfe6dc081ee5f245adcb115ed6ca1aa45ee50fa3f5",
      "source_file": "ASD-STE100_ISSUE9.txt"
    }
  },
  {
    "requirement": "You can use parentheses: - To make references to illustrations or text - To include letters or numbers that identify items on an illustration or in a text - To identify the work steps in a procedure - To include abbreviations - To give the singular and plural forms of a noun at the same time - To explain words or a part of a sentence - To include an alternative.",
    "rule_id": "8.3",
    "source": {
      "line_end": null,
      "line_start": null,
      "page": 107,
      "row": null,
      "source_digest": "sha256:a216fe199bd6e9c77fc743dfe6dc081ee5f245adcb115ed6ca1aa45ee50fa3f5",
      "source_file": "ASD-STE100_ISSUE9.txt"
    }
  },
  {
    "requirement": "In a vertical list, a colon (:) has the same effect on word count as a period and shows the end of a sentence.",
    "rule_id": "8.4",
    "source": {
      "line_end": null,
      "line_start": null,
      "page": 107,
      "row": null,
      "source_digest": "sha256:a216fe199bd6e9c77fc743dfe6dc081ee5f245adcb115ed6ca1aa45ee50fa3f5",
      "source_file": "ASD-STE100_ISSUE9.txt"
    }
  },
  {
    "requirement": "When you put text in parentheses, it counts as one word in that sentence.",
    "rule_id": "8.5",
    "source": {
      "line_end": null,
      "line_start": null,
      "page": 107,
      "row": null,
      "source_digest": "sha256:a216fe199bd6e9c77fc743dfe6dc081ee5f245adcb115ed6ca1aa45ee50fa3f5",
      "source_file": "ASD-STE100_ISSUE9.txt"
    }
  },
  {
    "requirement": "Count each of these elements as one word: - Numbers - Numbers together with units of measurement - Abbreviations - Alphanumeric identifiers - Quoted text - Titles, headings, placards, and labels - Proper nouns of individuals, groups, organizations, and geopolitical entities.",
    "rule_id": "8.6",
    "source": {
      "line_end": null,
      "line_start": null,
      "page": 107,
      "row": null,
      "source_digest": "sha256:a216fe199bd6e9c77fc743dfe6dc081ee5f245adcb115ed6ca1aa45ee50fa3f5",
      "source_file": "ASD-STE100_ISSUE9.txt"
    }
  },
  {
    "requirement": "Hyphenated words count as one word.",
    "rule_id": "8.7",
    "source": {
      "line_end": null,
      "line_start": null,
      "page": 107,
      "row": null,
      "source_digest": "sha256:a216fe199bd6e9c77fc743dfe6dc081ee5f245adcb115ed6ca1aa45ee50fa3f5",
      "source_file": "ASD-STE100_ISSUE9.txt"
    }
  },
  {
